Business Requirement Document (BRD)
Project Name: Food Delivery Application (Swiggy Model)
Document Version: 1.0
Date: October 10, 2026
1. Executive Summary
The purpose of this project is to build a comprehensive, multi-platform food ordering and delivery ecosystem similar to Swiggy. The platform will bridge the gap between customers, restaurant partners, and delivery personnel, delivering a seamless food ordering experience with real-time tracking, secure payments, and route optimization.
2. Project Scope
In-Scope
 * Customer Interface: Web and mobile platforms (iOS & Android) for searching restaurants, browsing menus, placing orders, and tracking deliveries.
 * Merchant/Restaurant Portal: Dashboard for managing menus, accepting/rejecting orders, and analyzing earnings.
 * Delivery Fleet Module: Mobile application for driver dispatch, real-time route navigation, order updates, and payout history.
 * Admin Control Center: Platform management tool for operational oversight, user management, order monitoring, dispute handling, and analytics.
Out-of-Scope (Phase 1)
 * Quick-commerce grocery delivery (e.g., Swiggy Instamart).
 * Genie/Courier pickup-and-drop service.
3. Stakeholders & User Roles
| Role | Key Description & Objectives |
|---|---|
| Customer | Searches for restaurants/dishes, places orders, makes payments, tracks orders, and provides feedback. |
| Restaurant Partner | Updates menu inventory, accepts incoming orders, prepares food, and marks orders ready for pickup. |
| Delivery Partner | Accepts delivery requests, picks up food from restaurants, and delivers to customer locations. |
| System Administrator | Manages users, onboarding, commissions, operational areas, platform fees, and platform-wide metrics. |
4. Key Functional Requirements
4.1 Customer Mobile & Web App
 * User Onboarding & Authentication: Signup/login via phone number (OTP), email, or social accounts.
 * Location & Search: Automatic GPS detection, manual address entry, filter by cuisine, rating, price, and dietary preference (Veg/Non-Veg).
 * Restaurant & Menu View: High-resolution dish photos, item customization (addons/variants), and real-time item availability.
 * Cart & Checkout: Promo code application, delivery tip selection, order summary breakdown (GST, packaging, delivery fee).
 * Payment Gateway Integration: Credit/Debit Cards, UPI, Mobile Wallets, Net Banking, and Cash on Delivery (COD).
 * Live Order Tracking: GPS tracking of the delivery partner on an interactive map from pickup to drop-off.
 * Ratings & Reviews: Dual rating system for food quality and delivery experience.
4.2 Restaurant Management Module
 * Order Management Dashboard: Real-time visual and audio alerts for new orders with options to accept/reject and set estimated prep times.
 * Menu Management: Enable/disable items dynamically, set pricing, update categories, and configure add-on packages.
 * Financial Performance: Daily earnings summaries, commission deductions, and payout history.
4.3 Delivery Partner App
 * Duty Toggle: Go online/offline to receive order allocations.
 * Order Dispatch System: Broadcast delivery alerts with pickup and drop distance/estimated earnings before acceptance.
 * In-App Navigation: Turn-by-turn map navigation integrated with Google Maps or MapmyIndia.
 * Order Status Updates: One-touch status changes: Arrived at Restaurant, Order Picked Up, Arrived at Location, Order Delivered.
4.4 Admin Console
 * User Management: Onboard and manage customers, restaurants, and delivery drivers.
 * Commission & Pricing Engine: Configure variable commission rates per restaurant, surge pricing, and distance fees.
 * Dispute & Refund Management: Customer support ticketing integration to process refunds and resolve disputes.
 * Analytics & Reporting: Revenue charts, peak ordering hours, heatmaps of active demand, and delivery SLA compliance reports.
5. Non-Functional Requirements
 * Performance: Maximum page load time under 2 seconds; search results delivered in less than 500ms.
 * Scalability: System architecture capable of handling up to 100,000 concurrent active users during peak hours.
 * Availability: 99.9% platform uptime with redundant server failovers.
 * Security: End-to-end SSL/TLS encryption, PCI-DSS compliance for payments, and strict adherence to data protection regulations (e.g., GDPR / India DPDP Act).
 * Localization & Accessibility: Multi-language support and high-contrast accessibility modes.
6. Success Metrics & KPIs
 * Order Completion Rate: ≥ 95% of initiated orders successfully delivered.
 * Average Delivery SLA: Under 35 minutes per order within standard operating zones.
 * Customer Retention: High 30-day repeat order rate.
 * App Store Ratings: Target score of 4.5+ stars across iOS and Android stores.
